    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jonathan Aranda** (67.88) leads the charge as our strongest play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Alcantara and a move to the #2 spot, which maximizes his opportunities for counting stats. **Lawrence Butler** (64.46) also provides elite value, as his plus-matchup against Burrows and favorable platoon split overcome the slightly negative park factors. While we typically prioritize SB upside, the daily efficiency scores suggest leaning into these high-probability contact hitters today, as the overall environment for stolen bases is suppressed by wind conditions in several contests. **Luis Arraez** (60.99) remains a core start for his high-floor contribution to our AVG category, though the wind blowing in at his venue slightly dampened his ceiling.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Geraldo Perdomo** (48.89), who was the first cut from our utility considerations. While he brings legitimate SB potential\u2014a primary focus for LawDog\u2014his lower raw projection relative to **Matt Chapman** (58.86) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (59.04) made him the odd man out; the optimizer favored their superior expected run production over the marginal speed advantage **Geraldo Perdomo** provides against Cavalli. We are also exercising extreme caution with our stars facing elite arms: **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (52.83) and **Taylor Ward** (48.72) face tough assignments against deGrom and Gausman, respectively. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** in particular sees his score suppressed by an elite SP skill penalty, but his reliability in the #2 hole necessitates his inclusion despite the risk.\n\nFinally, keep a close eye on the wind reports, which are actively penalizing our exposure to the Taillon matchup for **Luis Arraez**, **Drew Gilbert**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Matt Chapman**. With **Cal Raleigh** and **Will Smith** currently unavailable, we have limited flexibility should any late-inning defensive switches impact the bottom of our order. Ensure we are monitoring the status of **Tyler Freeman**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Gavin Sheets**, as these depth pieces remain on call should any of our starters be scratched prior to first pitch.",
